  "characterPolicy": "Approved source roster and owner uncertainty decisions retained. Persian pronouns او and ایشان, verbs, adjectives and occupations lack grammatical sex agreement; preserve explicit known identity through lexical words only at the original disclosure point. Never turn source masculine/feminine grammar evidence into new biological claims. For unknown phone/radio roles, use neutral role names and referent-preserving singular/plural expressions. Cat biological sex remains unestablished. Death keeps source feminine-reference evidence and poetic brother separately; Persian neutral pronouns do not erase the brother identity.",
  "terminologyDecisions": [
    "Guests = مهمان‌ها as the in-world threat; ordinary arrivals = بازدیدکنندگان and ordinary house guests = مهمانان معمول; no Persian capitalization exists, so context and glossary definition carry the distinction.",
    "Visitor-spirit = مهمان‌روح, a guest-derived compound coinage without the everyday party meaning of مهمانی; dead-person spirit = روح مرده. Distinct from مهمان; assertions remain attributed to the psychic service. All four occurrences read in full.",
    "КЧС = کمیتهٔ وضعیت‌های اضطراری; کوتاه form کمیته used only after clear identification. Original КЧС/FEMA/МЧС are quoted identifiers.",
    "For Rest, AURACAM, CR Channel / CR CHANNEL and internal codes retained literally. Named drink, beer and cigarette brands written in Persian script; never real brands.",
    "Resource انرژی has <sprite=0>; coffee increase has <sprite=1>; item numbers, next-day penalty and unspecified چند روز retained.",
    "All room, action, item and speaker distinctions reread throughout both fields. Inflection and singular/plural variation are intentional, not alternative concepts."
